<article class="env-corollary" id="BC7043">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BC7043">Corollary <span data-tag="BC7043">5.2.9.12</span>.</a> Let $\sigma : \Cat _{\infty } \rightarrow \Cat _{\infty }$ be an equivalence of $\infty $-categories, and let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category $($which we regard as an object of $\Cat _{\infty }$$)$. Then $\calC $ is equivalent to the nerve of a partially ordered set if and only if $\sigma (\calC )$ is equivalent to the nerve of a partially ordered set. </p>
